            <div xml:id="d751">

                <pb facs="0701" n="689" sameAs="frus:frus1944v05/pg689"/>

                <note rend="inline" type="source">800.51/1460: Telegram</note>
                <head>
                    <hi rendition="#italic">The Minister in Egypt</hi> (<hi
                            rendition="#italic">Kirk</hi>) <hi rendition="#italic">to the
                            Secretary of State
                    </hi>
                </head>
                <opener>
                    <dateline rendition="#float-right">
                        <placeName>
                            <hi rendition="#small-caps">Cairo</hi></placeName>, <date
                            calendar="gregorian" when="1944-04-21T14:00:00+03:00">April 21, 1944—2
                            p.m.</date>
                        <lb/> [Received April 21—12:45 p.m.]</dateline>
                </opener>
                <p>995. To Wallace Murray from Landis. Have been informed by the British that
                    Jordan, British Minister to Saudi Arabia, will be in Cairo next Monday for the
                    Middle East Financial Conference. They say that London after consultation with
                    you has instructed Jordan to discuss certain aspects of supply to Saudi Arabia
                    with me. In the light of the existing Saudi Arabian situation, I would be
                    pleased to receive any instructions that you may have on this matter.</p>
                <p>Sent London as No. 44 repeated Department as No. 995. [Landis.]</p>
                <closer>
                    <signed>
                        <hi rendition="#small-caps">Kirk</hi>
                    </signed>
                </closer>
            </div>
        </body>
    </text>
